ality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact declares no install steps and only requires git, though it documents a git-helper command without shipping an implementation in the inspected package.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The instructions mention mutating and networked Git operations, especially pull, push, and branch management, but they are presented as explicit user-invoked commands rather than automatic actions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistent services, hooks, scheduled tasks, credential harvesting, privilege escalation, or memory writes are present in the artifact.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is to expose common Git operations such as status, pull, push, branch, and log; those capabilities fit the skill's purpose.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you want the agent to help with Git operations. Treat push, pull, and branch management as state-changing actions: review the target repository and remote before asking the agent to run them.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: The scanner's concern about pull, push, and branch side effects is valid as user guidance, but the operations are explicit, purpose-aligned Git actions and the artifact does not show hidden or automatic execution.\n[AIG-SARIF] expected: The supplied static scan reported no results, which is consistent with the inspected Markdown-only artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789031106591}}}}}